 "_method": "THE BOX IS A CLIP BOX: ChatCut renders the graphic at the project canvas and the registered box CROPS it, so a box that is too small does not shrink the graphic, it CUTS it — and the cut reads as a broken component. Measured by rendering EVERY OTHER FRAME of the window over a flat #808080 plate and taking the bounding box of pixels that differ from the plate by more than 10 on any channel, then UNIONING across frames. Registered defaults and baked content are used, so the box describes what actually ships.",
 "_why_not_a_sample": "A component's extent is NOT MONOTONIC. RankedList peaks at f40 at 1058x654 and SHRINKS again to 652, 651, 650 — the bloom decays — and its four edges are set by FOUR DIFFERENT FRAMES (left f18, top f40, right f36, bottom f38). My earlier boxes were sampled at frames 15 and 45 and four came out too small for exactly this reason. Even the single largest frame under-measures PillCluster by 55px wide and 18px tall.",
 "_findings": {
  "RankedList": "Draws 1067px wide on a 1080 canvas and TOUCHES THE RIGHT EDGE (x1=1079) from f36 on — it overflows its own declared width prop of 1020 by ~47px. Rows enter in three steps: one row at f8 (h=184), two at f18 (426), three at f30 (630). A box measured before f30 misses a whole row, which is what row 1 surviving as a bare orange bar looks like.",
  "PillCluster": "It DRAWS — 890x297 centred — so the empty settled frame in ChatCut is not the component rendering nothing. Also note the registry carried width 1160 until today while the source said 1000, so any box measured before that fix was measured on a cluster that wrapped at a different width."
 }
}